    "turn_text": "You know, that's a great question. And let me tell you what happens. And I can talk to you about my evolution on all of this. I think when you first kind of get into politics, you know, I got to like the 10 years ago and I get there and I'm new to the place and all that. And so whether it's the people around you or just your own instincts, you sort of think, all right, you guys, yes, they're left of center and they're liberal. But at some point, there's some fairness in them, right? And so I think you waste a lot of time thinking you're going to impress people from in the legacy media. And I think that's worse than it's ever been in terms of their bias and so forth. And I think maybe one of the things that Donald Trump revealed is you're never going to impress these people. I mean, they're never going to treat you the same as they do the other side. I think once you abandon that and once you accept that that's a fact And then the next step is realizing, by the way, a lot of people notice, like there's a lot of people out there that notice the stubble standard. And so I always chuckle about things like, for example, you know, I, look, I ran for president. I finished in third place in the delegate count. I made it all the way to Florida. It didn't turn out the way I wanted it to, but that was God's plan for our country and for my life. And I, you know, things, there are a lot of things I've been able to do over the last four years. I wouldn't have been able to do if I had won that race or even been the nominee. And, you know, they call me up for a long time. They wrote about Marco Rubio failed presidential candidate. You know, Kamala Harris didn't even make it out of California. She didn't even make it to December.",
