    "turn_text": "Yeah, look, I think there's more than just Joe Manson and Chris and Cinema that don't want to get rid of the filibuster and think some of these ideas go beyond their comfort level. But if you watch what's happened to Joe Manchin and Kirsten Cinema when they stepped out, there's a lot of people that are saying, you know what, you know, I'm just going to vote with a pack and sort of keep my head down. It's not going to pass anyway. Thank God for Kirsten Cinema and Joe Manchin. And so these are people that are voting yes, but hoping for no. and the fact that two people are willing to step out and do it kind of give them the result they want it. But these guys don't, they don't want to be singled out. They don't want donors threatening them with primaries. They're scared. And so not saying that's true of everybody, but yeah, there are Democrats that do this is kind of crazy, but don't guys say it because their base has become radicalized. The people that knock on doors and make phone calls and that they need to mobilize for election day are demanding whatever the pet issue of the moment is. And they're far outside the mainstream. But if they take those people on, they may not be back. And they certainly don't want the headache associated with it. And so I think as much as anything else, the threats against Kirsten Senema and Joe Manchin that you've seen is not so much about Kirsten Senema and Joe Manchin. It's a message to the other senators and other members of Congress who may be thinking about stepping out a line that this is what awaits you. This is what lies ahead for you if you step out a line. So just be quiet and do what we tell you to do. And that's what I described.",
