    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "the easiest way to lose at anything is to think is to act like you're winning so i think that's the first thing we have to keep in mind the second is These guys raised a lot of money. As an example, Chuck Schumer went out and handpicked Val Demings, the Congresswoman from Central Florida, who was just a puppet of Nancy Pelosi and said, that's who I want to be our candidate in Florida. And she's raising $10 million a quarter or more online, just sending out an email. So they're going to raise that kind of money for candidates. I mean, every Senate Republican incumbent was out raised in 2020 and in 2018. So we can't overlook the fact that these people are going to out-raise us. We're also not going to get any benefit from media. As a perfect example, I was ranked the most effective Republican senator by the Vanderbilt University of Virginia program that looks at the effectiveness of members of Congress. Another group Again, nonpartisan ranked me the second number two in leadership score passed a bunch of really meaningful bills, not the least of which was the creation of the paycheck protection program that literally saved millions of small business jobs in this country. You wouldn't know that. I mean, we could go a couple of weeks ago. It was my work and having to blow up the defense bill that got force Nancy Pelosi in the house to pass. a bill that banned the import of products made by Uyghur slave labors. of that stuff is reported on. The media is a real challenge for us because they're not going to report on our accomplishments or accurately in many cases to put out what we're working on and what our position is on these issues. And so I wouldn't take that for granted either. So these guys are going to have more money and they're going to have the benefit of mainstream media. So we're going to have to work real hard to make sure that our base knows what's going on and that people turn out in both. Do I feel good about the direction of Florida? Do I feel good about the fact that people are realizing Joe Biden is a disaster? Absolutely. But the election isn't today. It's in November. We've got a long ways to go between now and then. We've got to make sure that people keep learning not just about what they're doing wrong, but what we're going to do right if they give us the chance to be in a position of control in the Senate House.",
