    "turn_text": "I mean, at the expense of sounding shameless, as I just pointed out, I mean, I've got an opponent running against me that's out raising the line, you know, donors from all over the country, honestly. He's MSNBC binge watchers that are sending stuff in the mail. So, I just ask people if they can to go on Marco Rubio dot com. Marco Rubio dot com and give whatever you can, because I need that help to get our word out and our message out. And I think beyond it, it's just to continue to be a platform like you've done where people can speak truth, where people can hear from the people, not just an office, but people that are in the periphery of politics, but who have opinions on these issues and a lot. It's become harder than ever. to have these sort of long-form conversations and nuanced conversations. So people can hear what we actually stand for and have debate. There's a disagreement about people stand for. Nowadays, it's harder than ever. I mean, it really is. I mean, you just can't get a message out anymore on legacy media. And it's platforms like this that are protecting the First Amendment and making that possible. So keep doing what you're doing with that floor to flare. Now that you're down here and talking about what really is happening down here, and hopefully that will inspire people across the country to elect the people and follow the direction that we've followed here.",
